The problem involves calculating the total number of trees planted by students and teachers in Ashley's school as part of a reforestation campaign. The school has 40 classes, each with an average of 25 students and 3 teachers. Each student plants 1 tree, and each teacher plants 2 trees.

First, calculate the total number of students:
$$ 40 \text{ classes} \times 25 \text{ students per class} = 1000 \text{ students} $$

Next, calculate the total number of teachers:
$$ 40 \text{ classes} \times 3 \text{ teachers per class} = 120 \text{ teachers} $$

Now, calculate the total number of trees planted by students:
$$ 1000 \text{ students} \times 1 \text{ tree per student} = 1000 \text{ trees} $$

Then, calculate the total number of trees planted by teachers:
$$ 120 \text{ teachers} \times 2 \text{ trees per teacher} = 240 \text{ trees} $$

Finally, add the trees planted by students and teachers:
$$ 1000 \text{ trees} + 240 \text{ trees} = 1240 \text{ trees} $$

Thus, the total number of trees planted at the end of the campaign is $\boxed{1240}$. 
