Now, he sold 10 goats from Farm X. So Farm X had 55, subtract 10. Let me write that down. Farm X: 55 - 10 = 45 goats left.

Then, he sold twice as many goats from Farm Y. The problem says "twice as many goats from Farm Y." Wait, so he sold 10 goats from Farm X, so twice that amount from Farm Y? So 2 times 10 is 20? Therefore, he sold 20 goats from Farm Y.

So Farm Y originally had 45 goats. Subtract 20. 45 - 20 = 25. 

