- The cost of one basket of **green food** is **$25**.
- The cost of one basket of **red food** is **$18**, but since you get **$2 off** for each basket of red food, the **discounted price is**:
  $$
  18 - 2 = 16 \text{ dollars}
  $$
- You are buying **3 baskets** of **both green and red food**, so:
  - 3 baskets of green food
  - 3 baskets of red food (each at the discounted price)

---

