To determine how many packs of glue sticks Mr. Jackson needs to buy, we can start by calculating the total number of glue sticks required. He has 27 students in his class and wants to give each student 2 glue sticks. Therefore, the total number of glue sticks needed is:

$$ 27 \times 2 = 54 \text{ glue sticks} $$

Next, we need to figure out how many packs of glue sticks are required to get at least 54 glue sticks. Each pack contains 8 glue sticks. To find out how many packs are needed, we divide the total number of glue sticks needed by the number of glue sticks per pack:

$$ \frac{54}{8} = 6.75 $$

Since Mr. Jackson can only buy whole packs of glue sticks and he expects to have some extra glue sticks left over, he needs to round up to the next whole number. Therefore, he will need to buy 7 packs of glue sticks.

$$ \boxed{7} $$

