$$
\frac{33}{3} = 11 \text{ dollars per hour}
$$

To determine how much she would earn after 12 hours at the same rate, we multiply her hourly rate by 12:

$$
11 \times 12 = 132
$$

We can also verify this by noting that 12 hours is 4 times 3 hours. Therefore, we multiply the earnings for 3 hours by 4:

$$
33 \times 4 = 132
$$

Both methods confirm that Ella would earn $\boxed{132}$ after 12 hours. 
